{title: 473 - Nearer My God, to Thee}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #473 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 473}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Nearer, [C7]my [Dm]God, [Bb]to Thee, Nearer [F/A]to Thee!
[C]E’en though [F]it [C7]be a [Dm]cross [Bb]That raiseth me,
[F/C]Still all my [C]song shall [C7]be,
[F]Nearer, my [Bb/F]God, to [F]Thee;
[F]Nearer, my God, to [Bb]Thee, [F]Nearer [C/E]to Thee!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Though like [C7]the [Dm]wanderer, [Bb]the [F]sun gone down,
[C]darkness [F]be [C7]over [Dm]me, [Bb]my rest a stone;
[F/C]yet in my [C]dreams I'd [C7]be
[F]nearer, my [Bb/F]God, to [F]thee;
[F]nearer, my God, to [Bb]thee, [F]nearer [C/E]to thee!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]There let [C7]the [Dm]way [Bb]appear, steps unto [F/A]heaven;
[C]all that [F]thou sendest [Dm]me, in [Bb]mercy given;
[F/C]angels to [C]beckon [C7]me
[F]nearer, my [Bb/F]God, to [F]thee;
[F]nearer, my God, to [Bb]thee, [F]nearer [C/E]to thee!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]Then, with [C7]my [Dm]waking [Bb]thoughts bright [F]with thy praise,
[C]out of [F]my [C7]stony [Dm]griefs [Bb]Bethel I'll raise;
[F/C]so by my [C]woes to [C7]be
[F]nearer, my [Bb/F]God, to [F]thee;
[F]nearer, my God, to [Bb]thee, [F]nearer [C/E]to thee!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[F]Or if, [C7]on [Dm]joyful [Bb]wing cleaving [F/A]the sky,
[C]sun, moon, [F]and [C7]stars forgot, [Bb]upward I fly,
[F/C]still all my [C]song shall [C7]be,
[F]nearer, my [Bb/F]God, to [F]thee;
[F]nearer, my God, to [Bb]thee, [F]nearer [C/E]to thee!
{end_of_verse}
